        "review": "The first game I've seen to capture the joy of pooping on company time. Legit one of my games of the year. It takes such a simple mechanic and elevates it through a deluge of tiny friction points that have you eking out every moment of efficiency. Try as you might to beat the system, you cannot win - just when you think you've got it figured, you'll find the boiling pot ever so slightly hotter. It does run a little long, especially as you spiral inevitably into debt and sickness. But its sharp satire of worker exploitation and conservative hypocrisy is cut with some lovely moments of worker solidarity.",
